%% Sequence diagram — Booking creation (AS-BUILT, schema v4)
%% Swimlanes follow the instructor deck (slides 13, 21, 29): User / UI (Gradio)
%% / Service / Database. Service layer: BookingService, PricingService,
%% AvailabilityService, CustomerService (logic tier). Data tier: DatabaseManager
%% (BEGIN IMMEDIATE transaction) + repositories, SQLite schema v4.
%% Config: hold 48h, grace 24h, buffer 60 min, deposit 30 percent.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User<br/>(Receptionist / Manager)
    participant UI as UI (Gradio)<br/>booking_views.py
    participant BS as BookingService<br/>booking_service.py
    participant PS as PricingService<br/>pricing_service.py
    participant AV as AvailabilityService<br/>availability_service.py
    participant DB as Database<br/>SQLite (schema v4)<br/>DatabaseManager

    U->>UI: Submit booking form<br/>(customer, hall, event type,<br/>package, start/end, guests, services)
    UI->>BS: create_booking(employee, customer_id,<br/>hall_id, start_at, end_at, ...)
    BS->>BS: require_permission("booking.create")<br/>+ validate inputs (ValidationError if bad)
    BS->>PS: calculate(hall_id, package_id,<br/>event_type_id, guests, services)
    PS->>DB: SELECT halls, packages, services,<br/>pricing_rules, discount_records
    DB-->>PS: catalog rows
    PS-->>BS: PriceBreakdown (itemised lines + total, piasters)

    BS->>DB: BEGIN IMMEDIATE
    Note over BS,DB: One write transaction (ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW 3.4 rule 1): expire overdue holds, check, re-check, insert, commit, or roll back everything on any failure.
    BS->>DB: Expire overdue holds<br/>(sweep_expired_holds: pending + hold_expires_at passed)
    BS->>AV: check_availability(hall_id, start_at, end_at)
    AV->>DB: SELECT bookings (hall, start, end, status)<br/>+ maintenance_blocks + hall_weekly_hours<br/>+ hall_special_hours + halls.status
    DB-->>AV: overlapping bookings, blocks, hours
    AV->>AV: Half-open [start, end) overlap + 60 min buffer<br/>+ hours + maintenance + closure + capacity
    AV-->>BS: AvailabilityResult (available / reason)

    alt Slot is free
        BS->>DB: Re-check availability immediately before commit
        BS->>DB: INSERT bookings (status pending,<br/>hold_expires_at = now + 48h)
        BS->>DB: INSERT booking_price_items (frozen price snapshot)<br/>+ booking_policy_snapshots + booking_history
        BS->>DB: INSERT audit_logs (same transaction, NFR-016)<br/>+ notifications (new_booking)
        BS->>DB: COMMIT
        DB-->>BS: booking row (number, id)
        BS-->>UI: Booking (Pending, hold until +48h)
        UI->>UI: gr.Info("Booking created, hold 48h")
        UI-->>U: Show Pending booking + deposit due (30 percent)
    else Slot is taken (conflict / maintenance / hours / closure)
        BS->>DB: ROLLBACK
        DB-->>BS: rolled back, no rows written
        BS-->>UI: raise BookingConflictError / HallUnavailableError
        UI->>UI: gr.Error("Hall unavailable: reason")
        UI-->>U: Show reason, offer another hall / time
    end

    Note over U,DB: Deposit step (same flow, later): record_payment inserts the payment,<br/>recomputes the paid total and, once the 30 percent deposit threshold is met<br/>inside the hold + 24h grace, auto-confirms the booking (BR-10), freezes the<br/>financial policy snapshot and generates the event plan, all in one transaction,<br/>and a failed step rolls back the payment too.
